summary:
  UPnP 716 in answer to a play is read as any other failure, so the widget
  says "Could not cast" of a device that works.

history:
  A Ruark R5se refused three station addresses with 716, "Resource not
  found", and played a fourth through the same helper a few minutes later
  (2026-11-12). "Could not cast to Ruark R5se. The device could not play
  this station." read as a speaker that is broken or off, and the listener
  had no way to know that the next station might just play. An answer that
  is about the resource is told apart now, and the widget says the device
  cannot play this station and that another may work.

target:
  package/contents/ui/CastLogic.js

find:
  var _REFUSALS = { "702": true, "703": true, "704": true, "714": true, "715": true, "716": true };

replace:
  var _REFUSALS = { "702": true, "703": true, "704": true, "714": true, "715": true };

expect:
  Killed by tests/qml/tst_castlogic.qml::test_what_an_answer_says.
